# Execution log — literature-structured-notes self-test
date: 2026-11-24
python: 3.12.14
dependency: PyMuPDF 2.1

## Test 1 — layout parser on a real paper
input: arXiv:1706.03762 (Attention Is All You Need), 15 pages
command: python src/parse_pdf.py test/attention.pdf execution/smoke/parsed
result: 540 blocks, 30 sections, 4 tables, 3 figures, 3 formulas, 0 uncertainties
evidence: parser prints the JSON summary; parsed.json/parsed.md hold the evidence layer

## Test 2 — note verifier (edge cases)
command: python src/verify_notes.py execution/smoke/note.json execution/smoke/parsed/parsed.json execution/smoke/verify
result: the verifier correctly flags a synthetic note's duplicate knowledge-point id
        (['kp1']) and a section missing its chapter summary (['s3']); all 11 claims'
        anchors resolve to real pages/sections/figures.
edge cases (separate run): page-out-of-range (p99), unknown figure id (fig99_0), and
        a 'reported'-confidence claim with no anchor are all flagged.

## Note
Both self-tests use a public paper and synthetic note JSON. The three official fixed
cases are supplied only by the evaluation platform and are NOT included in this bundle;
no formal test outputs or prepared answers are submitted.
